Rename RGB30 singleadc-joypad from retrogame_joypad

The upstream BSP labels the RGB30 singleadc-joypad node
"retrogame_joypad", a generic ODM string. Give it a device-specific
name so it appears distinct to userspace and does not collide with
unrelated retrogame_joypad devices.

Applied to both v1 (rk3566-rgb30-linux.dts) and v2
(rk3566-rgb30-v2-linux.dts) top-level DTS files.

Signed-off-by: James Pharaoh <james@pharaoh.uk>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-rgb30-linux.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-rgb30-linux.dts
@@ -126,7 +126,7 @@
 		compatible = "singleadc-joypad";
 		hw_info = <0x01>;
 
-		joypad-name = "retrogame_joypad";
+		joypad-name = "Powkiddy_RGB30_Controller";
 		joypad-product = <0x1101>;
 		joypad-revision = <0x0100>;
 
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-rgb30-v2-linux.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-rgb30-v2-linux.dts
@@ -126,7 +126,7 @@
 		compatible = "singleadc-joypad";
 		hw_info = <0x01>;
 
-		joypad-name = "retrogame_joypad";
+		joypad-name = "Powkiddy_RGB30_Controller";
 		joypad-product = <0x1101>;
 		joypad-revision = <0x0100>;
 
